<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Munuza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Munuza was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> governor of the Muslim conquerors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gijon">Gijón</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> in the early eighth century. According to the Asturian chronicles, the Visigothic noble Pelagius rebelled against him, and after the Muslim defeat at Covadonga Munuza fled and was caught and killed. The revolt against him marks the beginning of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturia">Asturias</a>.</p></div>
